# Tautomers: CREST finds the tautomers, xTB and DFT refine the lowest one.
recipe: tautomers
title: Tautomers
field: Conformations
summary: xTB optimisation, CREST tautomer search, then xTB, then DFT optimisation and frequencies of the lowest tautomer
description: xTB optimises the structure first because CREST needs an optimised geometry, CREST searches the tautomers and ranks them, xTB re-optimises the lowest and a DFT optimisation with frequencies refines it. The charge is that of the structure.
role: dft | DFT optimisation and frequencies | B3LYP | 6-31+G(d) | the usual starting level; diffuse functions when the molecule is an anion
rules: anion-diffuse, heavy-ecp, size, registered

variant: orca | CREST, xTB, ORCA | ORCA
step: orca | preopt | xtb | | Geometry | xTB Opt | structure
step: orca | crest | CREST | | Tautomers | tautomer search |
link: orca | preopt | crest | geometry
